## Full minimal example (v4)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre v4 – custom protocol demo</title>
  <script type="module">
    import maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.2.0/dist/maplibre-gl.esm.js';

    // 1️⃣ Register the protocol (static method!)
    maplibregl.addProtocol('mytiles', (params, abortSignal) => {
      const url = `https://my.tile.server/${params.z}/${params.x}/${params.y}.pbf`;
      return fetch(url, { signal: abortSignal })
        .then(r => {
          if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`Tile ${url} → ${r.status}`);
          return r.arrayBuffer(); // ← MapLibre expects raw bytes
        });
    });

    // 2️⃣ Create the map
    const map = new maplibregl.Map({
      container: 'map',
      style: {
        version: 8,
        sources: {
          mysource: {
            type: 'vector',
            tiles: ['mytiles://{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf'],
            // optional: minzoom / maxzoom, attribution, etc.
          },
        },
        layers: [
          {
            id: 'my-layer',
            type: 'fill',
            source: 'mysource',
            'source-layer': 'my_layer_name', // <-- name inside the .pbf
            paint: { 'fill-color': '#ff6600', 'fill-opacity': 0.5 },
          },
        ],
      },
      center: [0, 0],
      zoom: 2,
    });
  </script>
  <style>
    #map { position: absolute; top:0; bottom:0; left:0; right:0; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="map"></div>
</body>
</html>
```

**Key points**

* **Static registration** – `maplibregl.addProtocol`, not `map.addProtocol`.  
* **Return a value** (or a Promise) – never call a callback.  
* **Respect the abortSignal** – pass it to `fetch` (or check `abortSignal.aborted` if you do something else).  

