## Checklist – Did you miss any of these?

| ✅ | Item |
|----|------|
| ✅ | Call `maplibregl.addProtocol` **before** you instantiate any `new maplibregl.Map`. |
| ✅ | The handler returns **either** a `Response`, an `ArrayBuffer`, a `Blob`, a `Uint8Array`, or a `Promise` that resolves to one of those. |
| ✅ | The handler receives `(params, abortSignal)`. If you don’t need the signal, just ignore it, but **don’t drop the second argument** – otherwise MapLibre will think you’re using the old signature and will silently ignore the handler. |
| ✅ | If you still have the old `map.addProtocol` call, remove it (or keep it only for backward‑compatibility; it will be ignored in v4). |
| ✅ | Your tile URL template uses the new protocol name, e.g. `mytiles://{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf`. |
| ✅ | The returned data has the correct MIME type (`application/vnd.mapbox-vector-tile` for vector tiles, `image/png` for raster, etc.). |
| ✅ | You handle HTTP errors (throw or return `null`) so MapLibre can fall back to the “no‑tile” state instead of hanging. |

