## TL;DR code snippet you can copy‑paste

```js
import maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';

// 1️⃣ Register custom protocol (static!)
maplibregl.addProtocol('mytiles', (params, abortSignal) => {
  const url = `https://my.tile.server/${params.z}/${params.x}/${params.y}.pbf`;
  return fetch(url, { signal: abortSignal })
    .then(r => {
      if (!r.ok) throw new Error(`Tile ${url} → ${r.status}`);
      return r.arrayBuffer();          // ← return raw bytes
    });
});

// 2️⃣ Create the map (anytime after registration)
new maplibregl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: {
    version: 8,
    sources: {
      mysource: {
        type: 'vector',
        tiles: ['mytiles://{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf'],
      },
    },
    layers: [
      {
        id: 'my-layer',
        type: 'fill',
        source: 'mysource',
        'source-layer': 'my_layer_name',
        paint: { 'fill-color': '#ff6600', 'fill-opacity': 0.4 },
      },
    ],
  },
  center: [0, 0],
  zoom: 2,
});
```

That’s all you need to get your custom tiles back after the v3 → v4 upgrade. 🎉

